 35CA c  J|p=3/2+ for {+37}Ca ground state.                                     
 35CA c  2024Dr01: a 72-MeV/nucleon {+37}Ca secondary beam was produced via the 
 35CA2c  fragmentation of a 140-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ca{+20+} primary beam impinging
 35CA3c  on a 0.5-mm-thick Be target. Experimental setup includes the           
 35CA4c  CAESium-iodide scintillator ARray (CAESAR) for detecting |g rays, a    
 35CA5c  DSSD-CsI(Tl) |DE-E Ring Telescope for detecting protons, a             
 35CA6c  Scintillating-Fiber Array (SFA) and the S800 spectrograph for detecting
 35CA7c  heavy residuals. Measured E{-p}, E|g, and E(residual). Deduced the     
 35CA8c  first excited state in {+35}Ca via the 2p+{+33}Ar exit channel from    
 35CA9c  total decay-energy spectra using the invariant-mass method. Comparisons
 35CAAc  with shell-model calculations with the USDC Hamiltonian.               
